#
# THREE PROBE DEFECTS were found and fixed BEFORE this run; the numbers here are
# the post-fix ones, and they differ from the earlier truncated log on purpose:
#   1. upload fan-out re-sent one identical buffer, and uploadToWorkspace dedupes
#      on (workspaceId, sha256). 14 uploads created ONE document, so "publishes
#      x4 (distinct documents)" was really a second CAS race on one row and the
#      capacity table printed a shed that does not exist. Fixed by appending a
#      uuid comment per upload: uploads now 201 (15/20/39ms), not the 200 dedupe
#      hit at 5ms, and the row reports "documents=4 distinct of 14 uploaded".
#   2. the capacity generator grouped that CAS row under "publishes"; it is now
#      its own family, "revision conflict".
#   3. the refusal clock read the error panel only AFTER the 300x100ms poll gave
#      up, so every editor refusal was dated at the deadline (30830ms). Folded
#      the panel read into the poll: the 340-page document now reads
#      "refused after 238ms" - the product was always fast, the probe was slow.
#
